// The flags of the countries a person can have, for `PlayerName`: the drawing of each flag as
// an SVG text, and the Dutch name of the country for the text alternative. Every country of
// `countryCodes` (`@fansite/shared/countries`) has a name, and shows a flag or its code.
//
// There are three kinds of country (`flags.test.ts` checks that each country is one of them):
// - `flagDrawings`: the real flag, in at most 2048 bytes.
// - `simplifiedFlags`: the flag of a country whose real flag is too heavy, such as Spain or
//   Serbia, because of a coat of arms or fine detail. It has the colours and the layout of the
//   flag, without the arms, in at most 900 bytes. It is not the real flag.
// - `codeOnlyCountries`: no drawing, so `PlayerName` shows the two letters of the country in a
//   frame of the size of a flag.
//
// The real drawings come from flag-icons 7.6.0 (https://github.com/lipis/flag-icons, MIT licence,
// see `flag-icons-licence.txt` in this folder), format 4x3. To make them again, take
// `flags/4x3/<code>.svg` of the package. Put the shape that a `use` points to in the place of
// the `use`, so no drawing has a `use`. Then run svgo 3 on it with `multipass`, the
// `preset-default` with `removeViewBox` off, `floatPrecision: 0` in `cleanupNumericValues` and
// `convertPathData`, and `cleanupIds` with `minify`, and put the `xmlns` on the root. Keep the
// drawings of at most 2048 bytes. They are text in this file, and not files that a page asks
// for, so a flag costs no request, on the site, in Storybook and on the host alike.

